**Figure 1. Selected fits and the residual check.** Left: observations and fitted means for A (blue circles, solid OLS line) and B (orange triangles, dash-dot WLS line); the gray dashed line is the generating mean. Right: residuals from the initial OLS fit of each series, on one shared scale. B shows increasing spread with x; the supplied constant-variance design and residual check support OLS for A, while B uses WLS with inverse-variance weights $1/(0.5+0.15x)^2$. Lines are fitted means, not confidence bands. Coefficient intervals in the accompanying table are two-sided 95% Student-t intervals with 38 residual degrees of freedom and fitted residual scale; B uses the supplied variance shape as weights.
